WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.512
It’s October 4, 2018.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:16.224
The heat from the arena lights shine bright on the Tigers new head coach.

00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:19.561
It’s a coronation for the prodigal son of Memphis.

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:21.938
But for Penny Hardaway, this moment 

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:25.233
began years ago…with a wish from a dying friend.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:32.198
They became a closer-knit basketball team

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:36.411
with Penny coaching, but they knew all the time they was doing it for Dez

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:43.793
and it gave them the drive, the will. They wanted to win for Desmond.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.135
In the Binghampton area, it was tough because you had gangs,

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:53.887
negative things going on in the neighborhood, and you had 

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:57.891
to be really strong not to be a part of those negative things.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:01.269
I think kids growing up in Memphis, it was—it's different generations.

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:04.481
I grew up in the era where around my family there was hustlers,

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:07.859
being exposed to the life of street life, you know what I'm saying,

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:12.530
like, negative activity, hood life, you know, that a lot of people 

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.366
unfortunately can't get around because they born in these situations.

00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:22.082
Penny Hardaway was raised in Binghampton,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.084
a neighborhood east of downtown Memphis.

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:27.545
A few doors down lived Desmond Merriweather.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:32.675
As the two grew older they forged what would become a lifelong basketball bond

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:36.221
right here on these courts by Lester Middle School.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:42.143
We were probably—maybe 10, 11, 12 years old, somewhere in there

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:45.772
and we were in the park and I just knew Desmond, he was really competitive.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.901
Huge personality. Happy-go-lucky guy. Loved to laugh.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.402
But when it came to competing

00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:56.116
he would fight you to, I mean—he would fight you, honestly.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.743
If I get beat, I got to come back, I got to get revenge

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:01.704
because Dez now, he's small, but he's got a mouth.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.625
Dez was very competitive even though he was small in stature,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.877
and he would push Penny because he was saying

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:10.547
“You're bigger than me, you're stronger than me, can you take me?”

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:13.800
-It made me tougher. I didn't wanna lose either. It didn't matter if he was smaller

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.054
or not, I was gonna play him tough and didn't take it easy on him.

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:20.557
And he didn't want anybody to take it easy on him, so it helped both of us.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:28.606
Penny would go on to star at the high school, collegiate and pro levels.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.866
Dez played 4 years at Lane College in Jackson, Tennessee.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.995
After graduating he returned to their childhood neighborhood

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.206
to coach the Lester Middle School team,

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:47.667
the same middle school that both Dez and Penny attended.

00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:53.006
Dez loved the children, and I think he wanted to rush college

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:57.677
as fast he could just so he could get back here to coach children.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:01.639
Hard-nosed coach. You got to play hard to play for him can't be soft.

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:04.601
Had to be able to run through a wall for him if he asked you to

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.103
cuz he gives his all, so he expects that in return.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:11.357
He wasn't just teaching basketball. He was teaching morals and standards.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.819
The children really felt united and together and

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:17.447
they had a purpose, and once they got to winning,

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:22.744
the children, everything, they—their behavior changed.

00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:31.711
But just as the team started to thrive, Dez’s health began to decline.

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:38.259
One day he stopped by and I said, "Dez has lost a lot of weight."

00:03:38.259 --> 00:03:39.969
He said, "I have colon cancer."

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:45.391
I just passed out and he was like, "Mom, wake up. Please get up."

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:50.021
He looked at me and he said, "Mom, you know, I can't believe this.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:57.111
I am a person that do for everybody, anybody," and he said, "Me? Why me?"

00:03:57.111 --> 00:04:00.490
You know, so we sit there and we hugged one another and we both cried.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.784
With the cancer came along with the pain

00:04:02.784 --> 00:04:06.287
but Desmond still worked through that in games.

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:09.707
I could tell through his facial expression and stuff but

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:12.961
a lot of people in the audience and stuff didn't know what he was going through

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:14.921
but he was struggling to make it.

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:19.592
-He went through multiple surgeries. The second surgery

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:23.638
he wanted some paper and he scribbled on the paper one cent.

00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:25.974
I was like, "One cent?"

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:30.311
So Marty said, "Are you referring about Penny?"

00:04:30.311 --> 00:04:33.356
He couldn't speak because he was on the ventilator, he thumbsed up.

00:04:33.356 --> 00:04:38.736
He said call One Cent cuz he wanted him to, as sick as he was

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:44.409
he wanted Penny to coach the team for him, and that's what he was thinking about.

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:46.953
He needed somebody that he knew he can trust

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:49.747
and knew that not only would—

00:04:49.747 --> 00:04:52.583
he knew that Penny would teach them more than just basketball.

00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:57.088
His wife called me and said that Desmond was in the hospital

00:04:57.088 --> 00:05:00.341
and they had given him 48 hours to live. I'm like, "What?"

00:05:00.341 --> 00:05:04.220
I mean, he didn't have any signs or, if he did, he didn't tell anyone about it

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:10.059
and it went from no signs to going to the hospital and a routine checkup

00:05:10.059 --> 00:05:13.646
to see what was going on to, you know, like, stage 4 cancer.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.606
He smiled when he saw me come in and I kept

00:05:15.606 --> 00:05:19.277
saying to him, "Look man, let's get you well and we'll get to the basketball."

00:05:19.277 --> 00:05:22.071
He was like, "Naw man, I'm telling you, my middle school team,

00:05:22.071 --> 00:05:24.198
we're really good. He said, "Man, I know that you're the only guy

00:05:24.198 --> 00:05:27.702
that can save our neighborhood, and that's why I told them to call you.”

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:36.085
Dez recovered and Penny kept his pledge,

00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:38.629
staying to help Dez coach Lester Middle School.

00:05:40.631 --> 00:05:44.635
Even though the team was excelling, the kids were still being exposed

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:48.181
to the same dangers that Penny and Dez faced during their childhoods.

00:05:49.807 --> 00:05:55.021
The same thing goes on today. It's just it's faster because of the internet.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:58.316
It's because of the way the world's shifting with social media.

00:05:58.316 --> 00:06:02.070
So kids could also get exposed to a lot of things way early

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:06.115
and soon and not having to be directly in the household with it.

00:06:06.115 --> 00:06:08.201
Back then if you wasn’t directly with it

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:11.579
you wasn’t exposed till you heard about it.

00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:15.541
Now you can be directly exposed to it indirectly.

00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:20.463
Gang-banging, drug-dealing. Fighting all the time, killing.

00:06:21.464 --> 00:06:26.886
It's a lot of fighting. Police running around, gunshots. You see it all.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.765
Carpenter Street, you know what I'm saying, I can't,

00:06:30.765 --> 00:06:33.267
I can't cuz you know the police might go back and look at this.

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:34.060
I can't say it.

00:06:34.477 --> 00:06:38.523
Dez knew the territorial gang politics would always be a day-to-day struggle

00:06:39.357 --> 00:06:40.608
a challenge he met head on.

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:46.656
When I first got there, there were a couple kids that were in gangs

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:48.116
and it was distracting them.

00:06:48.116 --> 00:06:50.451
Dez thought that they were gonna get injured or killed

00:06:50.451 --> 00:06:54.705
so he went to the gang leaders and said, "Hey, you know,

00:06:54.705 --> 00:06:57.667
you see these kids from the basketball team, call me.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:58.876
They're not supposed to be here.

00:06:58.876 --> 00:06:59.669
We don't want them here.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:03.256
We want to get them a different path and we're going in a different direction.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:05.299
We don't want them to be a part of this gang."

00:07:05.299 --> 00:07:06.592
Everybody loved him.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.761
He had so much respect and love from around the neighborhood

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.263
that they, they granted him that wish.

00:07:12.181 --> 00:07:15.518
With the players protected Penny and Dez coached Lester Middle School 

00:07:15.518 --> 00:07:17.186
to 3 state championships.

00:07:18.187 --> 00:07:21.649
The basketball team helped him because he was living through the kids.

00:07:21.649 --> 00:07:23.484
He didn't know how much time he had, but he knew

00:07:23.484 --> 00:07:26.612
his love for those children and wanting to see them succeed

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.406
would help prolong his life, and it did.

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:36.122
Sunday, February 8th, 2015.

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:39.500
Penny got a text message that he knew one day was coming.

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:49.844
They texted me and said, "Hey, get to the house, you know, he's dying."

00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:52.555
And uh, went to the house right after church

00:07:52.555 --> 00:07:56.851
and as I was going through the door he was trying to speak.

00:07:56.851 --> 00:07:58.686
Desmond kind of like lifted his head up

00:07:58.686 --> 00:08:03.441
to tell Nikc that he love him and—

00:08:04.358 --> 00:08:07.570
then Penny came, and as sick as he was

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:11.282
he still was trying to, you know, hold his head up to look up

00:08:11.282 --> 00:08:13.493
to look at the end of the bed and tell him he loved him.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:16.579
-I could understand that he told me that he loved me back

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:18.915
and then all of a sudden it just went blank. He just went—

00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:21.626
two deep breaths and then it was over.

00:08:22.919 --> 00:08:26.589
Like it—I just witnessed that like, saying that I love you.

00:08:26.589 --> 00:08:27.965
He said he loved me 

00:08:27.965 --> 00:08:31.802
and then he just took two deep, deep breaths and then it just—

00:08:33.971 --> 00:08:34.805
that was it.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.768
Man, I couldn't believe it. I never witnessed anything like that

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:40.728
especially from a loved one, someone that I cared about.

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:47.026
To be able to witness that and to see what he had gone through up until that point,

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:51.030
it was almost like half of me was really sad

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.990
and the other half was "He's not in pain anymore."

00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:57.036
Desmond Merriweather died at the age of 41.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:09:00.039
The city of Memphis still mourns his loss.

00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:04.877
The grassroots basketball movement Dez generated

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:06.254
will be felt for generations

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:10.174
spawning some of the top high school and collegiate players in the nation.

00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:15.721
In our neighborhood he was the man, you know.

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:19.725
Everybody knew that he loved our neighborhood and he wanted it to do well.

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.644
He said our neighborhood needed a lift and

00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:23.854
he gave his heart and he gave his soul

00:09:23.854 --> 00:09:26.566
and his body and his life to those kids.

